# World-map tiles (16x16), 16-bit style: shaded terrain, dark outlines, 3-4 step ramps (light from top-left).
# Generated by a helper script (auto-shaded silhouettes + hand-placed details); edit freely.
#
# Palettes (15 colors each)
#   map.w1 .. map.w9  terrain + scenery of each world, same slot meaning in every world:
#       1 outline | 2 3 4 water deep/mid/light (open sky in W5, lava in W8) | 5 6 7 land light/base/shade
#       8 9 a alt ground light/base/shade (sand W2/W3, cloud W5, snow W6; flower petals W4)
#       b c d foliage light/base/dark | e trunk/bark | f white/sparkle
#   map.path   paths, dots, bridges, breakable rocks: 1 outline, 2-5 path base/light/shade/edge, 6-9 rock ramp,
#              a-c wood ramp, d rope/white, e f dot gold/orange.
#   map.panel  level panels + spade panel: 1 outline, 2 face, 3 face light, 4 face shade, 5 rim dark, 6 white,
#              7 8 red "M", 9 a spade navy/light.  (The engine draws the N-Spade/N-Spade card with its own palettes.)
#   map.icon   fortress, castle, Toad house, locks, airship, Hammer Bro, skull, start flag, pipe:
#              1 outline, 2 red, 3 white, 4 red light, 5 red dark, 6-8 stone ramp, 9 a gold, b c wood, d skin, e f green.
#
# Layering: terrain tiles (m.land m.land2 m.water1 m.water2 m.sand m.snow m.cloudland m.lava) are fully opaque.
# Every other map tile is an overlay with transparent surroundings, drawn on top of its cell's terrain
# (tiles tagged pal=map.w1 / map.w8 are drawn with the current world's map.wN).
# Paths: the path band is rows 5..10 (m.path.h) / columns 5..10 (m.path.v); m.dot and the panels reach the
# tile edges there, so paths join them seamlessly. m.dot also serves as the corner/junction piece.
# m.panel: the engine prints the level number in the 8x8 centre (x4..11, y4..11).
pal map.w1     #10280C #1848B0 #3088E8 #A8E8F8 #A0E870 #68C848 #40A038 #F8E8A8 #E8C878 #B89048 #88D858 #309838 #146020 #8A5028 #FFFFFF
pal map.w2     #3A1808 #1860B8 #3898E0 #B0E8F8 #F0C080 #D89850 #B07038 #F8ECC0 #F0D490 #D0A860 #A8D848 #58A830 #286818 #9A5A28 #FFF8E8
pal map.w3     #0C2040 #0C40A8 #2080E0 #98E8F8 #A8E878 #70C850 #48A040 #FFF8D8 #F8E0A8 #D8B878 #80E060 #38A840 #186828 #A86838 #FFFFFF
pal map.w4     #081808 #185898 #3088C8 #98D8E8 #68C050 #409838 #287028 #F890C0 #D05090 #882058 #60C848 #289030 #0C4818 #6A4020 #FFF8B0
pal map.w5     #282860 #6090F0 #88B0F8 #D0E4FF #B0E880 #78D060 #50A848 #FFFFFF #E0E0F8 #A8A8E0 #88E068 #40B048 #207030 #9A6038 #FFFFFF
pal map.w6     #101838 #183888 #3068C8 #A8E8F8 #C8D8F8 #8098D0 #506098 #FFFFFF #D8E4F8 #98B0E0 #70B8B0 #307878 #184848 #6A4838 #FFFFFF
pal map.w7     #0C0C14 #182838 #304860 #7898B8 #A0A0B8 #787890 #505068 #F8D878 #D8A840 #906818 #88A870 #507048 #283828 #604830 #E8F0FF
pal map.w8     #180606 #C02000 #F87010 #F8D030 #7A5E5A #584040 #382828 #A89898 #807070 #584848 #686058 #484038 #282018 #483020 #FFF8C0
pal map.w9     #100818 #280848 #483088 #8878C8 #6878A8 #485888 #304068 #C0B8D8 #9890B8 #686090 #6888A0 #406078 #203048 #504040 #F0E8FF
